{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20186",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.23,
      "end_seconds": 7.33,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "Uh, um, good evening, doctor, thanks for seeing me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.04,
      "end_seconds": 11.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.7,
      "end_seconds": 18.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I'm here with them in case I can help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.91,
      "end_seconds": 24.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.98,
      "end_seconds": 36.1,
      "duration_seconds": 10.12,
      "text": "Honestly, you know, it's some chest discomfort when I climb stairs, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.75,
      "end_seconds": 41.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.56,
      "end_seconds": 47.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "it's been going on for nearly five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.14,
      "end_seconds": 50.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "how much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.44,
      "end_seconds": 57.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "hmm, a seven out of ten, I suppose"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.01,
      "end_seconds": 62.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Alright, have you tried anything for it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.42,
      "end_seconds": 80.31,
      "duration_seconds": 16.89,
      "text": "Erm, only resting, and it's not much. Oh, um, and indigestion after tablets. That's been about the same, about a year. I mean, as for indigestion after tablets, I'd say mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.92,
      "end_seconds": 84.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "So, have you been feeling tired?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.86,
      "end_seconds": 87.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Yes, I have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.45,
      "end_seconds": 91.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.03,
      "end_seconds": 100.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.09,
      "text": "Pretty severe, if I'm being honest. I've also had bruising easily, for three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.75,
      "end_seconds": 109.08,
      "duration_seconds": 7.33,
      "text": "Have you had some chest discomfort when you climb stairs before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.64,
      "end_seconds": 116.1,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "I had a similar thing a couple of years ago. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.59,
      "end_seconds": 138.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "and what about blood in the urine, palpitations or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.03,
      "end_seconds": 144.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Right, um, none of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.08,
      "end_seconds": 147.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "And what about breathlessness or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.16,
      "end_seconds": 152.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "No, um, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.93,
      "end_seconds": 155.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.89,
      "end_seconds": 157.87,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "Breathing's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.62,
      "end_seconds": 162.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.57,
      "end_seconds": 165.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "no, that's all fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.63,
      "end_seconds": 169.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.35,
      "end_seconds": 171.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "No, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.25,
      "end_seconds": 176.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.96,
      "end_seconds": 184.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "My grandmother had dementia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.88,
      "end_seconds": 202.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.96,
      "end_seconds": 213.17,
      "duration_seconds": 9.21,
      "text": "I take metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day for my heart it's simvastatin, at night"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.99,
      "end_seconds": 216.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.34,
      "end_seconds": 223.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "20 milligrams. Glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 223.64,
      "end_seconds": 232.58,
      "duration_seconds": 8.94,
      "text": "I mean, uh, that's what's prescribed, but I'm not sure she takes it every day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.36,
      "end_seconds": 237.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.53,
      "end_seconds": 251.19,
      "duration_seconds": 11.66,
      "text": "I mean, I was told I'm allergic to plasters, but I don't remember what reaction I had. Tramadol, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.34,
      "end_seconds": 253.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.29,
      "end_seconds": 258.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "I have about eight cigarettes in a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.98,
      "end_seconds": 261.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.71,
      "end_seconds": 269.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.89,
      "end_seconds": 272.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.58,
      "end_seconds": 277.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.83,
      "end_seconds": 282.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "alright, are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.35,
      "end_seconds": 290.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.78,
      "end_seconds": 293.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.06,
      "end_seconds": 299.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.25,
      "end_seconds": 306.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.75,
      "end_seconds": 309.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "I've got heart disease"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.87,
      "end_seconds": 312.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "I see, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.27,
      "end_seconds": 317.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Yes, high cholesterol. Yes, diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.37,
      "end_seconds": 321.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.54,
      "end_seconds": 334.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "That's it, just a a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.29,
      "end_seconds": 359.46,
      "duration_seconds": 8.17,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 119 over 74, respiratory rate 18, temperature 36.7. And pulse 66, saturation 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 360.62,
      "end_seconds": 366.79,
      "duration_seconds": 6.17,
      "text": "Sorry, uh, what was I saying, is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.78,
      "end_seconds": 371.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Don't worry, we'll discuss it in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.76,
      "end_seconds": 376.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.31,
      "end_seconds": 386.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.22,
      "end_seconds": 390.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.62,
      "end_seconds": 408.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal and your chest is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 410.03,
      "end_seconds": 411.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 422.08,
      "end_seconds": 425.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "There are a few small bruises on your forearms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 427.72,
      "end_seconds": 428.7,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "sure thing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 434.08,
      "end_seconds": 449.37,
      "duration_seconds": 15.29,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. From what you've told me and what I found, my working impression is stable coronary disease on antiplatelet treatment, with minor bleeding. We shouldn't forget reflux from the tablets."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 450.8,
      "end_seconds": 454.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Actually, do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 455.96,
      "end_seconds": 479.61,
      "duration_seconds": 23.65,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's stable coronary disease on antiplatelet treatment, with minor bleeding, and we'll know more once the blood tests is back. Just to be sure I understood. You've had some chest discomfort when you climb stairs for nearly five years, and no breathlessness or blood in the urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 480.68,
      "end_seconds": 482.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Mm, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 483.37,
      "end_seconds": 504.22,
      "duration_seconds": 20.85,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange blood tests for bruising and bleeding. I'd like to arrange an ECG for chest discomfort. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I'm going to put you on pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast, long term. That's for stomach protection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 505.7,
      "end_seconds": 509.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "is that safe with my other medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 510.8,
      "end_seconds": 528.97,
      "duration_seconds": 18.17,
      "text": "Take your blood-thinning tablets after food and do not stop them on your own. If you pass black stools or have prolonged bleeding, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 529.8,
      "end_seconds": 532.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "no, that's all thanks a lot"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 534.9,
      "end_seconds": 536.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "goodbye for now"
    }
  ]
}